Title: The Last Light
Credit: Written by Jane Doe

FADE IN:

INT. OLD HOUSE - NIGHT

Rain hammers the windows. A single lamp flickers on the desk. The room
is small and dark, the kind of room that holds its breath.

ARTHUR (V.O.)
The night everything ended.

ARTHUR
I kept telling myself it was over. That the light would stay
gone. But it never does.

(beat)

ARTHUR
Not really.

CUT TO:

EXT. OLD HOUSE - NIGHT

The house sits alone at the edge of the woods. Its windows are dark
except one.

MARGO
You came back.

ARTHUR
Someone has to.

MARGO
Why?

ARTHUR
Because it's still there.
